# .dockerignore -- allowlist for the Docker build context.
#
# The context is everything the daemon receives, whether or not a COPY reads it.
# A deny-list has to anticipate every file that will ever appear in a checkout
# (local env files, editor state, caches, notes). An allowlist inverts that: nothing
# enters the context unless the Dockerfile needs it, so a new stray file is excluded
# by default.
#
# Keep this list equal to the COPY instructions in the Dockerfile. Adding a COPY
# there without adding the matching "!" line here fails the build with
# "file not found", which is the intended signal.

# Exclude everything.
*

# Dependency manifest (COPY requirements.txt in the builder stage).
!requirements.txt

# Application sources and migration config (COPY in the runtime stage).
!ledger.py
!worker.py
!provision.py
!alembic.ini
!alembic/

# Bytecode caches inside the allowed directories are machine-specific.
# These come after the "!" lines because the last matching rule wins.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
